  "study_summary": {
    "objective": "Compare Chinese (3.042) and Japanese (LBM 30007, LBM 30008) industrial soy sauce koji strains to find the proteolytic enzymes behind their different performance.",
    "experimental_design": "Each strain was grown as soy sauce koji (steamed soybean + wheat flour) and sampled at the mycelial expansion stage (30 °C) and the sporulation stage (28 °C); 3 replicates.",
    "main_finding": "Protease gene content barely differed between strains, but protease secretion and transcription did; combining phenotype and transcriptome data gave 58 candidate key proteolytic enzymes for koji fermentation."
  },
